   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general business law, in relation to prohibiting providers from imposing a fee for termination or early cancellation of certain service contracts in the event a customer has deceased before the end of such contract",
    "basePrintNo": "S6485",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6485-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §399-zzzz, Gen Bus L",
    "lawSection": "General Business Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6485\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the general business law, in relation to prohibiting\nproviders from imposing a fee for termination or early cancellation of\ncertain service contracts in the event a customer has deceased before\nthe end of such contract\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis bill would prohibit companies from charging early cancellation\nfees if a customer has deceased before the end of his or her contract.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Amends the General Business Law by adding a new section\n399-zzzz to prohibit providers of telephone, cellular telephone,\ntelevision, internet, energy or water services from imposing a\ntermination or early cancellation fee if a customer has deceased\nbefore the end of such contract.\n\nSection 2: Effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nMany companies use early termination fees to ensure a customer\ncontinues use of a service through the contract length. There have\nbeen instances where these companies have charged early termination\nfees to accounts cancelled prior to the expiration of the contract due\nto the customer's death. This legislation would prohibit the\nimposition of these fees in this circumstance.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to state.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
